The integration rewrites local imports to the sing-box module. The paired
server build restores the upstream import prefix and pins pion/turn v5.1.3.
See docs/vpnctl/turnrelay.md for the build command.

The relay uses the sing-box dialer, which applies DNS, detour and bind options.
The mux cancels allocation attempts and starts a new outbound generation on
path changes or prolonged silence. The exit owns its allocation handlers,
cleans up idle UDP associations, and flushes UDP reorder gaps on a timer.
Each client KCP connection closes its own FEC reader while UDP stays active.

Fork regression tests are named vpnctl_regression_test.go. The adapter exposes
static credentials in exit mode and requires an exit certificate pin for DTLS
and SRTP. The upstream VK provider, app, tray, commands and sing-box adapter
are outside the vendored subset.
